Subject: [PATCH] [vero5] Test bypass for odd-width unscaled YUV image conversion

Target Kodi 21.3 a3a448d plus the all/arm/vero5 series through 919.
The Moonraker 379x540 cache JPEG yielded different BGRA bytes only in
column 378 across otherwise identical loads, before ClampToEdge and GPU
upload. FFmpeg 6.0.1's generic unscaled yuv2rgb_c_32 handles 8/4/2 pixel
blocks, leaving an odd final column unwritten. Its selection requires
even height but does not exclude odd width. The ARM NEON unscaled path
requires width divisible by 16 and therefore cannot handle this case.

For the matching odd-width/even-height unscaled YUV420P/YUV422P/YUVA420P
image conversions, request SWS_ACCURATE_RND to exclude the generic fast
path. ConvertFormats already maps YUVJ420P/422P to these formats. Keep
the image dimensions, existing range handling and diagnostic snapshots.
Other image conversions retain SWS_BICUBIC. This is a targeted test
workaround, not a backport of an upstream FFmpeg fix; on-device validation
is required. Accurate rounding may change RGB values versus the fast path.

diff --git a/xbmc/guilib/FFmpegImage.cpp b/xbmc/guilib/FFmpegImage.cpp
--- a/xbmc/guilib/FFmpegImage.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/guilib/FFmpegImage.cpp
@@ -505,8 +505,26 @@
   nWidth = std::max(nWidth, 1u);
   nHeight = std::max(nHeight, 1u);
 
+  int swsFlags = SWS_BICUBIC;
+  // FFmpeg 6.0.1's unscaled YUV-to-RGB C fast path handles 8/4/2-pixel
+  // blocks but not a final odd pixel. Its selection checks for even height,
+  // not even width. Accurate rounding excludes that path without changing
+  // the requested dimensions or masking an unwritten edge with memset.
+  const bool oddUnscaledYuv =
+      (nWidth & 1) != 0 && (nHeight & 1) == 0 &&
+      nWidth == m_originalWidth && nHeight == m_originalHeight &&
+      (pixFormat == AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P || pixFormat == AV_PIX_FMT_YUV422P ||
+       pixFormat == AV_PIX_FMT_YUVA420P);
+  if (oddUnscaledYuv)
+  {
+    swsFlags |= SWS_ACCURATE_RND;
+    CLog::Log(LOGDEBUG,
+              "CFFmpegImage: odd-width unscaled YUV conversion bypass, {}x{}, format {}",
+              nWidth, nHeight, static_cast<int>(pixFormat));
+  }
+
   struct SwsContext* context = sws_getContext(m_originalWidth, m_originalHeight, pixFormat,
-    nWidth, nHeight, AV_PIX_FMT_RGB32, SWS_BICUBIC, NULL, NULL, NULL);
+    nWidth, nHeight, AV_PIX_FMT_RGB32, swsFlags, NULL, NULL, NULL);
   if (!context)
   {
     CLog::LogF(LOGERROR, "Could not create a scaling context for {} x {} pixels", nWidth,
